+  Scenario: isaac sessions set <id>.tags stores a vector of keywords as a set
+    Given default Grover setup
+    And the following sessions exist:
+      | name     | crew | tags |
+      | ops-room | main | #{}  |
+    When isaac is run with "sessions set ops-room.tags [:ops]"
+    Then the exit code is 0
+    When isaac is run with "sessions show ops-room --edn"
+    Then the stdout contains "#{:ops}"
+    And the exit code is 0
+    When isaac is run with "sessions list --tag ops"
+    Then the stdout contains "ops-room"
+    And the exit code is 0
+
   Scenario: isaac sessions set <id>.tags explains the set and member forms on bad input
     Given default Grover setup
     And the following sessions exist:
diff --git a/features/tagging/session_tags.feature b/features/tagging/session_tags.feature
index 3443156..4b41afd 100644
--- a/features/tagging/session_tags.feature
+++ b/features/tagging/session_tags.feature
@@ -97,6 +97,23 @@ Feature: Session tags
     And the stdout does not contain "sue"
     And the exit code is 0
 
+  Scenario: a session created with vector tags is selected by --tag
+    A vector (`[:ops]`) and a set (`#{:ops}`) are the same tags. The session
+    table, `sessions set`, and a hand-edited sidecar have all written the
+    vector, and `--tag` (and every other selector) has to see it.
+    Given default Grover setup
+    And the following sessions exist:
+      | name     | crew | tags   |
+      | ops-room | main | [:ops] |
+      | sue      | main | #{:project/poker} |
+    When isaac is run with "sessions list --tag ops"
+    Then the stdout contains "ops-room"
+    And the stdout does not contain "sue"
+    And the exit code is 0
+    When isaac is run with "sessions show ops-room --edn"
+    Then the stdout contains "#{:ops}"
+    And the exit code is 0
+
   Scenario: isaac sessions list --tag composes with --not-in-flight
     Given default Grover setup
     And the following sessions exist:
diff --git a/resources/isaac/agent/handbook.md b/resources/isaac/agent/handbook.md
index 5b6a59d..76d0a09 100644
--- a/resources/isaac/agent/handbook.md
+++ b/resources/isaac/agent/handbook.md
@@ -206,6 +206,12 @@ in-progress turn marker, fire-and-forget).
   creation when a real match exists and isn't itself busy; if you need to
   always land on one session, name it explicitly with `session`. See
   Frequencies, below, for the full picture.
+- **A tagged session is missed by `sessions list --tag`, a hail, or a
+  space's `session-tags`.** Tags are a set of keywords. A vector in
+  `session.edn` or in a session table (`[:ops]`) is the same set as
+  `#{:ops}` — Isaac reads them as a set, and `sessions set <id>.tags
+  [:ops]` stores `#{:ops}`. A session written the old way is selected
+  without rewriting the file.
 - **`history-retention` doesn't seem to match what I just set on the
   crew.** It's resolved once, at session creation, and locked — changing
   the crew's default afterward doesn't retroactively change existing
